      "created_at": "2021-03-24T20:14:42Z",
      "updated_at": "2021-03-24T20:14:42Z",
      "body": "Yes the cookie issue is becoming more and more important in meeting various laws across the globe. More and more governments are introducing privacy/cookie laws of various strengths so we need the ability to be able to micro manage all EE cookies to meet requirements.\r\n\r\nIdeally a fresh EE install wouldn't set any cookies by default (aside from CP related cookies which fall under strictly necessary), we'd then be able to enable them as needed with parameters as JCogs suggests, either via the Consent module or implied consent (which can sometimes be fine). \r\n\r\nWe need to stay as current as possible with laws. If EE doesn't adapt here it could soon prevent new developers coming on board?",
