      "created_at": "2021-03-25T01:34:19Z",
      "updated_at": "2021-03-25T01:34:19Z",
      "body": "building on @blue-dreamer comment there may be a case for EE to put itself at the extreme end of the compliance spectrum since it seems different countries enforce privacy regulations differently - discussion in Slack suggests that GDPR in Belgium and Germany is more stringently enforced than in UK - e.g. apparently logs of all consent decisions (even ones where consent is anonymously declined) are required. Not sure how we find / define the boundary conditions, but probably makes sense for an assumption of 'implement the more private case as a default' and 'keep better logs' options should be general principles to inform decisions.",
